# Build context excludes. The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so anything left here
# lands in an image layer and is pushed to the registry — keep secrets out.
#
# ⚠ WRITE DIRECTORY PATTERNS WITHOUT A TRAILING SLASH (`venv`, not `venv/`).
# azure-cli's tar packer (acr/_archive_utils.py, class IgnoreRule) only strips a
# trailing slash for `!` negation rules, so `venv/` compiles to the regex
# `^venv/$` and matches neither the directory entry nor its children — az then
# uploads the whole thing. That was silently sending ~471 MB of venv per build.
# Docker itself treats `venv` and `venv/` alike, so the slashless form is correct
# for both. (`.git` and `.venv` escaped the bug only because _archive_utils
# hardcodes them.)

# secrets — MUST stay excluded (env is injected by the k8s Secret at runtime)
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.pfx

# vcs / editors
.git
.gitignore
.idea
.vscode
.claude

# python
venv
.venv
__pycache__
*.py[cod]

# local runtime state — rebuilt in-container, synced from Azure Blob
data/faiss
data/hashes
data/docs
data/*.db
documents.db
sessions.db

# ACR Tasks writes a temp <hash>_Dockerfile into the uploaded context
*_Dockerfile

# not needed at runtime. NOTE `*.html` only matches root level (both docker and
# az compile it to a non-slash-crossing pattern), so templates/*.html — which
# app.py serves via Jinja2 — still ships. Do not "fix" this to **/*.html.
docker-compose.yml
*.html
README.md
